-# PRD-0001 — public landing page. Brand-neutral first pass (drift flag: the
-# design-sprint brand tokens land later as a restyle). No paid-tier promises,
-# no external network calls, no real-person likeness. The loop explanation is
-# ≤5 bullets, and the CTA points at the PRD-0002 sign-up route.

%section.landing-hero.bg-base
  %h1.font-display.text-display.font-bold.tracking-display TGenetics
  %p.landing-tagline.mt-4 Genetic algorithms as a service — an evolution loop you run against your own fitness function.

%section#how-it-works.mt-16.md:mt-24
  %p.landing-kicker.font-data.text-caption.font-medium.tracking-caption.uppercase.text-signal.mb-2 The Loop
  %h2.font-headline.text-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-4 How it works
  %ol.landing-steps.mt-6.space-y-3
    %li We suggest an organism to test — drawn at random from the organisms you haven't scored yet.
    %li You test it on your infrastructure, against your fitness.
    %li You report one number: the fitness you measured.
    %li We breed offspring — crossover and mutation — from the outcomes.
    %li Repeat: every generation gets more informative.

%section#trust.mt-16.md:mt-24
  %p.landing-kicker.font-data.text-caption.font-medium.tracking-caption.uppercase.text-signal.mb-2 Your fitness
  %h2.font-headline.text-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-4 Your fitness function stays yours
  %p We never run or evaluate your fitness function. You test every suggestion on your own infrastructure, and the only number we see is the one you report.

%section#pricing.mt-16.md:mt-24
  %p.landing-kicker.font-data.text-caption.font-medium.tracking-caption.uppercase.text-signal.mb-2 Pricing posture
  %h2.font-headline.text-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-4 Pricing
  %p.landing-tier-label Free tier — the basic loop
  %p.landing-tier-desc.mt-3 Suggestions, one fitness number per suggestion, and offspring breeding. Free while we learn who really needs this.
  %p.landing-paid-note.mt-4 A paid tier is planned for later. Nothing about it is built or promised yet.

%section#what-is-a-ga.mt-16.md:mt-24
  %p.landing-kicker.font-data.text-caption.font-medium.tracking-caption.uppercase.text-signal.mb-2 What is a genetic algorithm?
  %h2.font-headline.text-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-4 An evolution loop that searches your design space
  %p
    A genetic algorithm is an evolutionary loop: we vary candidate solutions, you test them,
    the best ones get selected, and we breed the next round. Variation → test → selection →
    repeat. Each cycle searches a design space for candidates that score well against a
    fitness function — the one number per candidate that measures what you actually care about.
  %p.mt-4
    The fitness function stays yours. We never run or evaluate it — you test every suggestion
    on your own infrastructure and report one number back.

%section#use-cases.mt-16.md:mt-24
  %p.landing-kicker.font-data.text-caption.font-medium.tracking-caption.uppercase.text-signal.mb-2 Use cases
  %h2.font-headline.text-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-4 Where one number per candidate is enough
  .use-case-cards.grid.grid-cols-1.gap-4.lg:grid-cols-3
    .use-case-card
      %h3.font-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-2 Payment form tips
      %p.mt-3
        A tip amount is a genome: three amounts you tune. We suggest a configuration, your
        checkout measures the one number that matters, and we breed the next generation of tip
        suggestions.
    .use-case-card
      %h3.font-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-2 Design parameter search
      %p.mt-3
        Any product with a recipe — layout, thresholds, component sizing — where each candidate
        can be scored. We propose, you measure on your box, we evolve toward better candidates.
    .use-case-card
      %h3.font-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-2 Hyperparameter selection
      %p.mt-3
        Pick a set of numeric knobs for a model or process, score each combination once, and let
        the loop find the region worth exploring next — one reported number per trial.

%section#create-a-genome.mt-16.md:mt-24
  %p.landing-kicker.font-data.text-caption.font-medium.tracking-caption.uppercase.text-signal.mb-2 Create a genome
  %h2.font-headline.text-headline.font-semibold.tracking-headline.mb-4 From blank chromosome to first suggestion
  %p
    A genome is a set of typed alleles that define the value space you want to search. The designer
    lets you build one with four allele types: Float, Integer, Boolean, and Option. Set a
    population size and evolution thresholds, turn it into an experiment, and request your first
    suggestion.
  .landing-shots.grid.grid-cols-1.gap-4.sm:grid-cols-2
    %figure.landing-figure
      %picture.landing-picture
        %source{media: '(min-width: 640px)', srcset: image_path('designer-desktop.png')}
        = image_tag 'designer-mobile.png', alt: 'Chromosome designer — typed alleles for Float, Integer, Boolean and Option', class: 'landing-shot w-full rounded-md border border-line'
      %figcaption Build a chromosome from typed alleles.
    %figure.landing-figure
      %picture.landing-picture
        %source{media: '(min-width: 640px)', srcset: image_path('experiment-desktop.png')}
        = image_tag 'experiment-mobile.png', alt: 'Experiment workspace — configuration, population and fitness trend', class: 'landing-shot w-full rounded-md border border-line'
      %figcaption Turn it into an experiment and request a suggestion.

